#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:3
#: 91f91f8bb95e413b937810b05a15c4f9
msgid "Qubes builder details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:8
#: 61144893db664e989527946b0abc24ad
msgid ""
"**Note:** This information concerns the old Qubes builder (v1). It supports "
"only building Qubes 4.1 or earlier.The build process has been completely "
"rewritten in `qubes-builder v2 <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-builderv2/"
">`__      . This can be used for building Qubes R4.1 and later, and all "
"related components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:11
#: 2e45bff975564ce1b31c1976b4aef278
msgid "Components Makefile.builder file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:14
#: d2ce3ec2d52a4d8d91d3dec2b373b14f
msgid ""
":doc:`QubesBuilder </developer/building/qubes-builder>` expects that each "
"component have *Makefile.builder* file in its root directory. This file "
"specifies what should be done to build the package. As name suggests, this "
"is normal makefile, which is included by builder as its configuration. Its "
"main purpose is to set some variables. Generally all available variables/"
"settings are described as comments at the beginning of Makefile.* in :doc:"
"`QubesBuilder </developer/building/qubes-builder>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:16
#: 8246e014635f4cdd9bfbc058a1bf9cb9
msgid "Variables for Linux build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:18
#: 20c096fe340f48d18c6d816827d7df38
msgid ""
"``RPM_SPEC_FILES`` List (space separated) of spec files for RPM package "
"build. Path should be relative to component root directory. :doc:"
"`QubesBuilder </developer/building/qubes-builder>` will install all "
"BuildRequires (in chroot environment) before the build. In most Qubes "
"components all spec files are kept in *rpm_spec* directory. This is mainly "
"used for Fedora packages build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:20
#: 4e21480af987457aa3d9a13f00b03fcd
msgid ""
"``ARCH_BUILD_DIRS`` List (space separated) of directories with PKGBUILD "
"files for Archlinux package build. Similar to RPM build, :doc:`QubesBuilder "
"</developer/building/qubes-builder>` will install all makedepends, then "
"build the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:24
#: a4614c968f494938a183cfea3c5011ea
msgid ""
"Most components uses *archlinux* directory for this purpose, so its good to "
"keep this style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:26
#: 5baa43c39602423aac454810f717c05f
msgid "Variables for Windows build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:28
#: 793758b26263498fa8c48bc4dbec162e
msgid ""
"``WIN_COMPILER`` Choose which compiler should be used for this component, "
"thus which build scripts. Currently two options available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:30
#: 9c8070f95b444285a5929c3e03e455cd
msgid ""
"``WDK`` - Windows Driver Kit (default). Command used to build: *build -cZg*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:32
#: 45680ea2ba6747afaab9f2d047157a5c
msgid "``mingw`` - MinGW (Windows gcc port). Command used to build: *make all*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:36
#: c39d77627f2f4f5ea1014bbe96b61896
msgid ""
"``WIN_SOURCE_SUBDIRS`` List of directories in which above command should be "
"run. In most cases it will be only one entry: current directory (*.*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:38
#: 9e38d89ee03e4c0fbe0e9b0001ca8d8b
msgid ""
"``WIN_PREBUILD_CMD`` Command to run before build, mostly useful for WDK "
"build (in mingw case, you can use makefile for this purpose). Can be used to "
"set some variables, preprocess some files etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:40
#: 5a0a67c749da4989b761ee447c5d2493
msgid ""
"``WIN_SIGN_CMD`` Command used to sign resulting binaries. Note that default "
"value is *sign.bat*. If you don’t want to sign binaries, specify some "
"placeholder here (eg. *true*). Check existing components (eg. vmm-xen-"
"windows-pvdrivers) for example scripts. This command will be run with "
"certain environment variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:42
#: e1049ff9af1c4cc18f8c32279b2d547e
msgid "``CERT_FILENAME`` Path to key file (pfx format)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:44
#: 2b8db020d6f846dfbc1bad5d8360d605
msgid "``CERT_PASSWORD`` Key password"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:46
#: 93a6a93d69874c528faf6d7789ffd403
msgid ""
"``CERT_PUBLIC_FILENAME`` Certificate path in the case of self-signed cert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:48
#: 9f2ce209cd9948ff9a4d0ff530a32cb2
msgid ""
"``CERT_CROSS_CERT_FILENAME`` Certificate path in the case of correct "
"autheticode cert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:50
#: 5c5aa8dfbd4346229bb50f706f2b96b8
msgid "``SIGNTOOL`` Path to signtool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:54
#: bc4e3dd21dea4ecab72f941ea9ce0a61
msgid ""
"``WIN_PACKAGE_CMD`` Command used to produce installation package (msi or "
"msm). Default value is *wix.bat*, similar to above - use *true* if you don’t "
"want this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:56
#: ab03509a81284840b2fdd9d6311c2901
msgid ""
"``WIN_OUTPUT_HEADERS`` Directory (relative to ``WIN_SOURCE_SUBDIRS`` "
"element) with public headers of the package - for use in other components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:58
#: 95693ebdc8124fbf96c1955c50db7b87
msgid ""
"``WIN_OUTPUT_LIBS`` Directory (relative to ``WIN_SOURCE_SUBDIRS`` element) "
"with libraries (both DLL and implib) of the package - for use in other "
"components. Note that :doc:`QubesBuilder </developer/building/qubes-"
"builder>` will copy files specified as *$(WIN_OUTPUT_LIBS)/\\*/\\** to match "
"WDK directory layout (*<specified directory>/<arch directory>/<actual "
"libraries>*), so you in mingw build you need to place libraries in some "
"additional subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:60
#: cc76ca5539354d2d9a333501cc7944ab
msgid ""
"``WIN_BUILD_DEPS`` List of components required to build this one. :doc:"
"`QubesBuilder </developer/building/qubes-builder>` will copy files specified "
"with ``WIN_OUTPUT_HEADERS`` and ``WIN_OUTPUT_LIBS`` of those components to "
"some directory and provide its path with ``QUBES_INCLUDES`` and "
"``QUBES_LIBS`` variables. Use those variables in your build scripts "
"(*sources* or *Makefile* - depending on selected compiler). You can assume "
"that the variables are always set and directories always exists, even if "
"empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:65
#: 2cbd4c7182eb45f9ac08e3b700416d5d
msgid "builder.conf settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/building/qubes-builder-details.rst:68
#: 8f322ec87b624bb2b9891b44b4f01b3d
msgid ""
"Most settings are documented in *builder.conf.default* file, which can be "
"used as template the actual configuration."
msgstr ""

